+ *
+ * Evidence (cci_burst_trace.txt, wide session 2558.143..2558.339, 14376
+ * writes): the stream is 16 back-to-back packets. Each packet's trace gap
+ * equals its own bus time at ~9.5 us/write — so the "~63 ms inter-burst
+ * pause" recorded in FINDINGS 9 was a burst-index misread (burst[4] occupies
+ * that window; there is no idle gap). Only four gaps exceed the bus-time
+ * model and carry real settles: ~24 ms after the power-up packet, and
+ * ~5/15/6 ms around the AE + stream-on group. The 0xFFFF blocks are real
+ * 929-byte data-port writes (a 0x3288 bank-select write precedes each), not
+ * delay pseudo-entries — they stay in the stream untouched.
+ *
+ * Single variable vs v33: engine setup (reset + timing) runs ONCE per packet
+ * instead of once per 28-entry chunk, the vendor's packet boundaries are
