+		 * lane bank read back as nine zeros (ctrl0=0xe, refgen=0xd5 and
+		 * common1138 were normal) and which then showed rx=0x70000 with
+		 * rdin=0. Make that condition loud so the next boot can confirm
+		 * or refute it instead of inferring it from a log diff. */
+		/* v95: vendor `csiphy_3ph_v2_4_0_reg` starts with {lane+0x94 = 0x0d}
+		 * (the C-PHY lane mode word) and `csiphy_reset_exit_reg_2_4_0` says
+		 * {0x1000 = 0x02, delay 10}, while this driver writes 0x1000=0x0E and
+		 * never writes 0x94. Read both back so one boot can tell whether the
+		 * lane bank is dead because the lane mode word / reset state diverges
+		 * from vendor (cf. the 11-20 17:36 boot: nine lane reads all zero). */
+		printf("PANDORA SLICEB: v95 phy-state %s reset1000=%#x "
+		    "lane94=%#x/%#x/%#x\n", phase, pc_rd(phy0, 0x1000u),
